    "document": "Core Rules",
    "section": "13. Terrain",
    "ruleNumber": "13.05",
    "summary": "Dense Terrain is substantial enough to shield models from enemy sight. Examples include ruins, woods and buildings. A terrain area containing a dense feature is Obscuring. See Hidden and Solid for their rules on dense terrain.",
